---
import Base from '~/layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, legalEntityIN } from '~/lib/site';
const updated = '2026-05-05';
const entity = legalEntityIN;
---

<Base
  title="Cancellation & Refund Policy · India"
  description={`Cancellation and refund policy for ${entity.name} digital product purchases on the India variant of ${site.domain}.`}
  pageType="WebPage"
  noindex={false}
>
  <section class="container-app py-20 max-w-prose-tight">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal · India</p>
    <h1 class="mt-4">Cancellation &amp; Refund Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-subtle text-fluid-sm">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-subtle text-fluid-sm">
      Applicable to purchases made on the <code class="font-mono text-xs px-1 py-0.5 rounded bg-surface-2">/in/</code> variant of {site.domain} (INR pricing, Razorpay checkout). Read alongside our <a class="text-brand" href="/in/legal/terms">Terms of Service</a>.
    </p>

    <div class="prose mt-10 text-muted [&_h2]:text-fg [&_h2]:mt-10 [&_h2]:mb-3 [&_h2]:text-fluid-xl [&_h3]:text-fg [&_h3]:mt-6 [&_h3]:mb-2 [&_h3]:text-fluid-base [&_p]:my-3 [&_strong]:text-fg [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-6 [&_li]:my-1.5 [&_a]:text-brand">

      <p class="text-fluid-sm">
        This Cancellation &amp; Refund Policy is a computer-generated
        electronic record published in terms of Rule 3 of the
        Information Technology (Intermediary Guidelines and Digital
        Media Ethics Code) Rules, 2021 (as amended) read with the
        Information Technology Act, 2000.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Nature of the products</h2>
      <p>
        All products sold by <strong>{entity.name}</strong> through
        <code>{site.domain}/in/</code> are <strong>digital products</strong>
        — source-code repositories, configuration packages, and access to
        a private community channel — delivered electronically immediately
        on payment confirmation. They are not subject to physical
        shipping (see our separate <a href="/in/legal/shipping">Shipping
        &amp; Exchange Policy</a>).
      </p>

      <h2>2. Cancellation</h2>
      <p>
        Because delivery is automatic and immediate, an order
        <strong>cannot be cancelled</strong> after the Razorpay payment
        is captured and the buyer has been granted access to the
        purchased repository or community channel. If You initiated a
        payment but it has not yet been captured (for example, an
        abandoned UPI prompt), no further action is needed — the
        authorisation will expire automatically and no funds will be
        deducted.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Refund — free Vibe Coder Kit</h2>
      <p>
        The free Vibe Coder Kit involves no payment and therefore
        carries no refund. You may unsubscribe from the associated
        email communications at any time using the unsubscribe link in
        any marketing email or by writing to
        <a href={`mailto:${entity.email}`}> {entity.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Refund — individual paid agents (BSK-001 to BSK-006)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Eligible for a <strong>full refund within 14 days</strong> of purchase.</li>
        <li>Reason is not required, but a one-line explanation helps us improve.</li>
        <li>Request the refund by <strong>replying to Your Razorpay receipt</strong> or by emailing <a href={`mailto:${entity.email}`}>{entity.email}</a> from the email address used at checkout.</li>
        <li>After 14 days, no refunds are issued, in line with the digital-goods nature of the Service.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Refund — AI Digital Marketing Stack bundle (BSK-ALL)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Eligible for a <strong>full refund within 7 days</strong> of purchase. The shorter window reflects the substantially higher value at risk on bundle purchases where the entire six-agent source delivery is granted immediately.</li>
        <li>Same request channel as individual agents (reply to receipt or email <a href={`mailto:${entity.email}`}>{entity.email}</a>).</li>
        <li>After 7 days, the bundle is non-refundable.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. How refunds are processed</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Approved refunds are issued via Razorpay back to <strong>the original payment instrument</strong> only — credit card, debit card, UPI VPA, or net-banking account used at checkout. We cannot redirect a refund to a different instrument.</li>
        <li>Refund initiation typically takes <strong>1 working day</strong> from approval; settlement to Your bank or wallet typically takes a further <strong>5 to 7 working days</strong> depending on the issuing bank's settlement cycle.</li>
        <li>Where Razorpay's "Optimum" speed is requested, settlement may be faster but is subject to a small additional fee borne by us, at our discretion.</li>
        <li>You will receive a Razorpay refund-confirmation email containing the refund reference ID. If the funds do not appear in Your account within 10 working days of that email, contact <a href={`mailto:${entity.email}`}>{entity.email}</a> with the refund reference and we will follow up with Razorpay.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>7. Effect of refund</h2>
      <p>
        On any refund being approved and initiated, the following
        consequences take effect immediately:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your access to the private GitHub repository for the refunded SKU is revoked.</li>
        <li>Your role in the Glitch Grow Discord server (<code>@Agent Buyer</code> or <code>@AI Digital Marketing Stack Buyer</code>) is removed, and access to the corresponding paid channels is closed.</li>
        <li>Your entitlement to lifetime updates for the refunded SKU is terminated.</li>
        <li>The Business Source License 1.1 ("BSL") under which the agent was delivered <strong>terminates</strong> with effect from the refund date. Any continued use, deployment, or onward delivery of the previously-licensed source after that date constitutes infringement.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These consequences are described here so they are not a
        surprise — they are the inevitable mirror of a refund and apply
        regardless of whether the refund was initiated by You or by us.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Disputes &amp; chargebacks</h2>
      <p>
        Before initiating a card chargeback or UPI dispute, please
        contact us at <a href={`mailto:${entity.email}`}>{entity.email}</a>
        — we will issue a refund directly per Sections 4 and 5 above
        wherever Your request falls within the eligibility window. If a
        chargeback is filed against an ineligible transaction, we will
        contest it with Razorpay using the records of access delivery
        (repository invitation, Discord role assignment, IP and
        timestamp logs).
      </p>

      <h2>9. Grievance redressal</h2>
      <p>
        If a refund request is not handled to Your satisfaction, or if
        You believe an approved refund has not been credited within the
        timeframes above, You may escalate to our Grievance Officer:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Grievance Officer</strong>: {entity.owner} (proprietor)</li>
        <li><strong>Email</strong>: <a href={`mailto:${entity.email}`}>{entity.email}</a></li>
        <li><strong>Postal address</strong>: {entity.address}</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We acknowledge such complaints within 7 working days and respond
        within 30 days, in accordance with the IT Rules, 2021 and the
        DPDPA, 2023.
      </p>
      <p>
        For payment-instrument-related disputes specifically, You may
        also approach Razorpay's grievance channel at
        <a href="https://razorpay.com/grievances/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"> razorpay.com/grievances</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        This Policy is governed by the laws of {entity.jurisdiction}.
        Any dispute is subject to the dispute-resolution mechanism set
        out in our <a href="/in/legal/terms">Terms of Service</a>
        (arbitration seated at {entity.arbitrationSeat}; courts at
        Gwalior, Madhya Pradesh have exclusive jurisdiction over
        matters not subject to arbitration).
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
